      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The core test is simple — encode a 36-byte zero-filled `ByteBuffer` to hex and verify the result — but the class is cluttered with many unused imports, fields, and helper methods. I'll improve understandability by:\n\n1. Removing all unused imports, fields, and helper methods\n2. Naming the magic numbers as constants\n3. Making the expected value self-documenting`String.repeat()` requires Java 11+. I'll fix the expected value using a compatible approach.The project's Java version doesn't support `String.repeat()`. I'll replace it with a `StringBuilder`-based static initializer that's equally clear.The test compiles successfully. The improved version removes all unused imports, fields, and helper methods, and replaces the opaque 72-character string literal with named constants and a self-documenting static initializer that makes the \"36 bytes → 72 hex chars\" relationship explicit."
